# Default owner for everything.
* @kalisam

# Invariant-touching surfaces. In the consensus gateway's own vocabulary these
# are "Substrate" blast radius -- but note what this file does and does not do.
# CODEOWNERS assigns owners to paths and requests their review. It does not
# enforce an approval threshold and it does not prevent a bypass; that is branch
# protection, configured in repository settings, and it is not set up yet. Nor
# do these rules add an independent reviewer today, since the default rule and
# every rule below name the same owner. They are here so the paths are declared
# and so branch protection has something to point at.
/ARF/dnas/                      @kalisam
/docs/adr/                      @kalisam
/docs/specs/spec-registry.json  @kalisam
/.github/                       @kalisam

# Shared-surface manifests. Every one of these is materialized outward into
# per-harness projections (Claude, Codex, Gemini, Hermes, OpenCode). Editing a
# projection instead of its manifest is always a mistake; editing a manifest
# changes what every harness sees.
/shared-agent-memory-surface.json  @kalisam
/shared-agent-surface.json         @kalisam
/shared-ai-roster-surface.json     @kalisam
/shared-context-surface.json       @kalisam
/shared-hook-surface.json          @kalisam
/shared-skill-surface.json         @kalisam
